# What a merchant does NOT receive.
#
# This file has to live INSIDE the package directory, not only at the repository
# root: `git archive` reads .gitattributes from within the tree it is archiving,
# so in a monorepo a root-only file governs a whole-repo archive nobody
# publishes while every real per-package zip still ships everything below it.
Test/ export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
# THIS SAID phpunit.xml.dist, AND NO SUCH FILE EXISTS.
#
# The rule named a thing nothing checks, so it silently did nothing and
# phpunit.xml shipped to every merchant - measured in the artefact, not the
# working tree: `git archive HEAD | tar -t` carried both packages' phpunit.xml
# among 439 entries. The neighbouring phpstan and phpcs rules DO end in .dist
# and were correctly excluded, which is the discriminator.
#
# It is worse than untidy. The shipped phpunit.xml declares
# bootstrap="Test/bootstrap.php" and <directory>Test/Unit</directory>, and BOTH
# are export-ignored - so a merchant receives a test configuration pointing at
# paths that are not in their vendor tree. The same shape as export-ignoring
# docs/ and stranding the images it referenced.
#
# The file was later renamed to phpunit.xml.dist, the name the CI gate and
# PHPUnit itself look for; every documented command passes `-c phpunit.xml.dist`.
# A developer's own uncommitted phpunit.xml override stays excluded too.
phpunit.xml.dist export-ignore
phpunit.xml export-ignore
phpstan.neon.dist export-ignore
phpcs.xml.dist export-ignore
